 "insights": [
  {
   "text": "Opening Sunday is the least predictable day of the week: a typical 6h 40m in 2025 versus 1h in 2024. The difference was weather, not demand \u2014 treat the two years as separate scenarios rather than averaging them."
  },
  {
   "text": "Wait times during the first 36 hours after opening can be five or more hours.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://burningman.org/black-rock-city/preparation/getting-there-and-back/gate/",
   "years": [
    2023,
    2024,
    2025,
    2026
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "If you can arrive Tuesday or later, you will find your wait time to be much shorter.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://burningman.org/black-rock-city/preparation/getting-there-and-back/gate/",
   "years": [
    2023,
    2024,
    2025,
    2026
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "On all days but opening night, the shortest lines are usually in the early morning hours, generally from 3 a.m.-10 a.m.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://burningman.org/black-rock-city/preparation/getting-there-and-back/gate/",
   "years": [
    2023,
    2024,
    2025,
    2026
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Heavy traffic and longer wait times indeed happen Saturday, Sunday and Monday.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://journal.burningman.org/2016/05/black-rock-city/building-brc/getting-to-and-from-black-rock-city-takes-time-and-patience/",
   "years": [
    2016
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Gate Road travel times during Exodus peaked at six to nine hours just to get from Greeters to the pavement of County Road 34.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://survival.burningman.org/transportation-traffic/exodus/",
   "years": [
    2024,
    2025
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Allow up to 12 hours to reach the Reno airport during peak egress (Exodus).",
   "sourceUrl": "https://survival.burningman.org/transportation-traffic/exodus/",
   "years": [
    2026
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Best exodus windows: try to leave very early in the morning, in the later evening, or on Tuesday morning before noon.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://survival.burningman.org/transportation-traffic/exodus/",
   "years": [
    2026
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "For 2026 Burning Man is aiming for a maximum ingress travel time - from the gravel to the Gate - of four hours whenever possible.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://journal.burningman.org/2026/03/black-rock-city/participate-in-brc/gate-improvements-2026/",
   "years": [
    2026
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Waits of 6+ hours once you get to the playa are common at peak arrival hours (Sunday mid-day through Tuesday night, with ebbs and flows within that time period).",
   "sourceUrl": "https://www.burn.life/getting-to-burning-man-entry.html",
   "years": [
    2017,
    2018,
    2019,
    2022
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "If you arrive from about Wednesday onwards, you're not going to have any real problems with entry lines.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://www.burn.life/getting-to-burning-man-entry.html",
   "years": [
    2017,
    2018,
    2019,
    2022
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Even if you have Early Entry passes you can still expect to wait half an hour to a couple hours at gate.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://www.burn.life/getting-to-burning-man-entry.html",
   "years": [
    2017,
    2018,
    2019,
    2022
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "In 2014, some people waited upwards of 18 hours in line after the gate was closed due to rain.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://www.burn.life/getting-to-burning-man-entry.html",
   "years": [
    2014
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Arriving before the 12:01am opening is actively punished: early arrivals without credentials are staged behind on-time drivers. In 2019, arriving at 11:49pm meant ~5 hours; arriving one minute later meant 25 minutes.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://www.trippingly.net/directions-to-burning-man-portland",
   "years": [
    2019
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "2023 was the mud-year anomaly: the driving ban meant Exodus, not ingress, was the extreme. Exodus ran 5h10m -> 6h -> 8h through Monday Sept 4 evening and was still ~7.5h Tuesday morning.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://www.newsweek.com/burning-man-update-exodus-wait-time-travel-information-road-reopens-1824485",
   "years": [
    2023
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "2024 opening was weather-shifted: the gate closed for rain and reopened around 3:15pm Saturday, roughly 12 hours after closure, with ~20,000 people waiting.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://www.sfchronicle.com/california/article/burning-man-rain-19721005.php",
   "years": [
    2024
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "2025 was the worst modern ingress year in this dataset: an Aug 23 windstorm (45-50+ mph gusts) closed the gate, and the backlog produced 6-9 hour official waits through Monday Aug 25 and into Tuesday Aug 26.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://www.2news.com/news/local/burning-man-gates-reopen-6-9-hour-wait-to-enter-black-rock-city/article_aa2210c0-84d7-4a32-916f-9fcd45959cc6.html",
   "years": [
    2025
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Reported wait is self-defeating: when the reported Gate Road travel time is low, many folks choose that moment to leave, which can increase those times faster than they can be reported.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://survival.burningman.org/transportation-traffic/exodus/",
   "years": [
    2026
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "More than one third of Burners arrive on the first Monday of the event; a quarter still arrive after Monday, peaking again on the Thursday.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://blackrockcitycensus.wordpress.com/2014/05/01/burning-man-related-variables-how-do-people-arrive/",
   "years": [
    2013,
    2014
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Early Arrival (work access) holders are ~12% of the population and enter before 6pm Sunday; in 2018 the Early-Arrival-only line still ran 2-4 hours on the Thursday/Friday/Saturday before opening.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://x.com/bmantraffic/status/1033005050665291776",
   "years": [
    2018
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Averaged over 2014-2017, ingress wait peaks roughly 18-26 hours after the gate opens (Sunday evening into Monday pre-dawn) at about 5 hours, is near zero in the first 2-4 hours after opening, and shows a second smaller ~2.5h bump around 58-62 hours after opening.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://www.trippingly.net/burning-man-transportation-logistics",
   "years": [
    2014,
    2015,
    2016,
    2017
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Averaged over 2014-2017, Exodus wait is low until the Temple burn (~24h after Man burn), then rises to a 3-4 hour plateau across the following 12-36 hours.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://www.trippingly.net/burning-man-transportation-logistics",
   "years": [
    2014,
    2015,
    2016,
    2017
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "2024 ingress collapsed to a flat 20-minute floor from event Wednesday onward and never exceeded 30 minutes from Thursday to Burn Saturday.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://www.bmantravel.com/data.js",
   "years": [
    2024
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "2025 ingress stayed at or above 6 hours from Opening Sunday 09:00 through Tuesday 06:00 almost continuously, peaking at 8h40m on Monday 10:00.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://www.bmantravel.com/data.js",
   "years": [
    2025
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Exodus peaks Sunday night (Temple Sunday ~20:00-23:00) and again Monday evening; the Tuesday-after window collapses to ~25-45 minutes.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://www.bmantravel.com/data.js",
   "years": [
    2024,
    2025
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "BMIR 94.5 / GARS 95.1 FM broadcast hourly Gate Road wait reports at the top of the hour; @bmantraffic posts the same numbers, which is why hourly series exist at all.",
   "sourceUrl": "https://survival.burningman.org/transportation-traffic/arriving-at-brc/",
   "years": [
    2016,
    2018,
    2019,
    2022,
    2023,
    2024,
    2025
   ]
  }
 ],
